      "tree_id": "8c6dabd73e520a272b24b5fed0f5a23ff82621a9",
      "message": "Derivation report: read an issue's author when no board row names it; a README is not code\n\n#54 (darkhipo, 2026-10-24, average sensitivity 37619/10000) changed only the constant of\nAnchen0823's #49 proof and was not held, because of two gaps in the report:\n- an Other bounds row has no board file, so the corpus had no author for issue #49 and an\n  unknown author never holds. The corpus now reads the issue's submitter (one GET per issue\n  entry, cached, inside the report budget); an unreadable issue leaves the author unknown.\n- a changed README counted as a non-constant change. README, NOTICE and other credit files now\n  count for the credit lines only; Lean code alone decides constants-only.\nProbe on the real #54 sources (2026-10-24): closest #49, 35 of 42 files identical, constants-only,\ncredit kept, hold: yes (20 reads). #54 itself stays listed (lead released it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
